<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle roundup  - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle roundup  - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said trade was quiet late Friday. There were no sales of slaughter steers or heifers confirmed at the close.</p>
<p>Inquiry and demand were moderate. Feedlots were very current. Few available cattle priced at $70.00 to $71.00, bids $69.00, last established prices were $69.00 on Thursday, Feb. 27. Last week 95,500 head confirmed including 18,900 head or about 20 percent previously contracted or formulated cattle.</p>
<p>confirmed: </p>
<p>none     last week:  100	  last year: 2100</p>
